## 2. Functional requirements & business rules

### 2.1 Data extraction (scraper)

- [x] Extract first 30 entries from `tr.athing` rows
- [x] Entity fields: `number` (int), `title` (string), `points` (int, default 0), `comments` (int, default 0 for “discuss” or missing)
- [x] Edge cases covered in tests (missing score, “discuss”, “1 comment”, no comments link)

### 2.2 Word-count logic

- [x] Words split strictly by whitespace (`\s+`)
- [x] Isolated symbols/punctuation excluded
- [x] Example verified: `"This is - a self-explained example"` → exactly **5** words

### 2.3 Filters & ordering (strategies)

- [x] `MORE_THAN_5_WORDS_BY_COMMENTS` — > 5 words, sort by comments desc
- [x] `LESS_OR_EQUAL_5_WORDS_BY_POINTS` — ≤ 5 words, sort by points desc
- [x] Strategies do not mutate the input array
- [~] **Observation:** added extra filter id `NO_FILTER` (no strategy; returns all entries in original order) for the default UI view and Worker endpoint

### 2.4 Telemetry & audit

- [x] Collection `usage_logs` with `timestamp` (ISO 8601)
- [x] `filter_applied`
- [x] `results_count`
- [x] `execution_type`: `"MANUAL"` | `"SCHEDULED"` | `"ORDER"` | `"SEARCH"` (validated; invalid values rejected)
- [x] `execution_time_ms`
- [~] **Observation:** save reasons also include human-readable strings for scrape-only runs (`Scraping and save entries (manual)` / `(each 2 h)`)
- [~] **Observation:** UI actions audit via `POST /api/logs` with `ORDER` (`Order by points` / `Order by comments`) and `SEARCH` (`filter by [n] words`)

